{
  "_comment": "Conformance cases for capturing a call against a compiled plan. `plan` has two MCP tools on one host and an HTTP operation on another, their records reading the body, the query and path segments; each case is that plan with `patch` applied (RFC 6902: add, remove, replace), and `call` what the callout hands over: its :authority, :method and :path as sent, its body as text or `{\"unread\": <why>}`, and `body_bytes`, the body's length as sent (its text's when absent). `expect.taken` is the record counting the call: `{\"entry\": <id>}`, or `{\"catch_all\": <id>, \"why\": ...}` with why: `no_entry`, `unmatchable: <why>`, or where the walk stopped, `refused <entry>: <refusal>`, `ambiguous <entry>`, `body_unread <entry>: <why>`. Whichever record it is, `keys` holds each of its context keys' readings (`{\"method\": ...}`, `{\"host\": ...}` or `{\"unparseable\": <why>}`, `{\"path_prefix\": ...}`, or a path's), and `measures` request_bytes and each named measure's, one reading per path: `{\"string\": ...}`, `{\"replaced\": <why>}`, `{\"not_a_string\": null}`, `{\"found\": <bytes>}`, `absent`, `ambiguous`, `{\"body_unread\": <why>}`.",
